  "page1": {
    "title": "Who, Where, and What Happens",
    "subtitle": "A short story shows us its character, its setting, and its event.",
    "body": "Here is a short story. On a rainy afternoon, a boy named Jun walked home through the park. Under a bench, he found a small puppy, wet and shaking. Jun had no umbrella, so he wrapped the puppy in his jacket. He carried it to a warm shop and asked for help. The shopkeeper smiled and gave the puppy some milk.\n\nNow let's find the three parts of this story. The character is the person <mark>the story follows</mark>. Here, the character is Jun, the kind boy. The setting is the time and place. The setting is a park on a rainy afternoon. The event is the main thing that happens. The event is that Jun saves the lost puppy. When you can name the character, the setting, and the event, you understand a story.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/05.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A boy named Jun wraps a shivering puppy in his jacket in a rainy park."
  },
